The fresh four-target build and manifest verification passed, but the new native smoke exposed a real harness race: it sent SIGTERM and immediately closed stdin, allowing EOF to win and produce exit 0 before the signal handler’s required exit 130. That is exactly the kind of cleanup-boundary bug this task is meant to catch. I’m fixing the harness to keep stdin open until the terminated process exits, then I’ll stress the signal path repeatedly.
